# Timestamped snapshots of the user's real shell login file, written before every
# edit. These are machine-local recovery artifacts, not source:
#   - they are snapshots of a personal ~/.zshrc, which is exactly where API keys
#     and tokens tend to live, so committing them creates a standing pipeline
#     from "shell config" to "git remote"
#   - a fresh one is written on every sync, so they accumulate without bound
#   - they are only useful on the machine they came from
backups/

# Byte-compiled Python (the tool is run directly, never imported).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The data tables live in the data dir ($WAYPOINT_DATA, default ~/.config/waypoint), never here.
/waypoints.md
/launches.md
/layouts.md
*.bak*
